    "body": "### Terraform Version\r\nTerraform v0.8.4\r\n\r\n### Affected Resource(s)\r\n- aws_iam_policy_attachment\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nSo what's happening is that I run my terraform config from a clean state (nothing set up) and it sets up everything correctly.  However, if I run it again, when I'd expect it to exit with nothing to do, this happens:\r\n\r\n```\r\n~ module.api_server_instance_profile.aws_iam_policy_attachment.policy_to_profile_attachment.2\r\n    roles.#:          \"2\" => \"1\"\r\n    roles.2808959860: \"api-server\" => \"api-server\"\r\n    roles.397096961:  \"bastion\" => \"\"\r\n\r\n~ module.bastion_instance_profile.aws_iam_policy_attachment.policy_to_profile_attachment\r\n    roles.#:          \"2\" => \"1\"\r\n    roles.2808959860: \"api-server\" => \"\"\r\n    roles.397096961:  \"bastion\" => \"bastion\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nThen I run `apply` again and it does this:\r\n\r\n```\r\n~ module.api_server_instance_profile.aws_iam_policy_attachment.policy_to_profile_attachment.2\r\n    roles.#:          \"0\" => \"1\"\r\n    roles.2808959860: \"\" => \"api-server\"\r\n\r\n~ module.bastion_instance_profile.aws_iam_policy_attachment.policy_to_profile_attachment\r\n    roles.#:         \"0\" => \"1\"\r\n    roles.397096961: \"\" => \"bastion\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nThen I run it again and it does the first one.  It just keeps going back and forth like that.\r\n\r\n### Debug Output\r\nI've generated the debug output for the `plan` when it should be doing nothing, but instead removes the policy attachment.\r\n\r\nI'm not willing to paste this publicly but if you give me an email address to send it to, I have it in a secret gist.\r\n\r\n### Expected Behavior\r\nNothing.\r\n\r\n### Actual Behavior\r\nSee \"Description\" above\r\n\r\n### Steps to Reproduce\r\n1. `terraform apply`\r\n\r\n### Important Factoids\r\nThis has been happening for a very long time.  I think since the resource was introduced.\r\n\r\n### References\r\nNone that I could find",
